    {
      "id": "claim_80da0a0292354baebbf837dc315f44f8",
      "statement": "Relay escalation to the optional implementation-strong role is one C at a time and is triggered only by the review result (the C failing review escalateAfter times in a row) or by the plan's own [strong] annotation combined with the cheap implementer's escalate=true report, never by the Hub judging difficulty itself; the next C after an escalated one always reverts to the cheap implementation role. Every message the Hub injects into a relay child or sends to the parent is prefixed with [relay <short id> <plan basename>] so multiple concurrent relays are never confused with each other.",
