    {
      "id": "claim_0d6b505785fb4b4f868decbd30fac3f5",
      "statement": "relay.json is rewritten on every state transition and is the relay's source of truth for surviving a Hub restart, recording state, round counters, completed Cs, child session IDs, roles, branch, worktree path, last verdict, and a timeline; the working relay files (board.md, child-<id>.md, review-c<k>-r<r>.md, relay.json) live under ~/.many-ai-cli/orchestration/<orchestration_id>/, and a relay stops for a round limit, timeout, missing verdict/review file, blocked verdict, child exit, or the Stop button, resuming only when the stop reason is resumable.",
